---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Terms & Conditions" description="Terms and Conditions of New Life Integration & Wellbeing Network CLG.">
    
    <section class="bg-linear-to-b from-teal-950/40 via-background to-background pt-20 pb-12 text-center relative border-b border-border/40">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10">
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary tracking-wider uppercase mb-2 block">📋 Service Agreement</span>
            <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground mb-4">Terms & Conditions</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
                Please read these terms and conditions carefully before using our website and services.
            </p>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-muted-foreground/60 mt-3 font-medium">Last updated: May 27, 2026</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground space-y-6">
            
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">1. Introduction</h2>
            <p>
                By accessing and using the website and services of <strong>New Life Integration & Wellbeing Network CLG</strong> ("we", "us", "our", "NLI"), you accept and agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions. If you do not agree to these terms, you should not use our website or services. These terms apply to all visitors, users, event attendees, programme participants, branch applicants, and volunteers.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">2. About Our Organization</h2>
            <p>
                New Life Integration & Wellbeing Network CLG is a Company Limited by Guarantee (CLG), registered in the Republic of Ireland. As a CLG, we are a not-for-profit organisation established to support individuals and families in their integration journey across Ireland. For any operational or official inquiries, please contact: <a href="mailto:info@lifeintegration.ie" class="text-primary hover:underline font-semibold">info@lifeintegration.ie</a>.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">3. Use of Our Website</h2>
            <p><strong>Acceptable Use:</strong> You agree to use our website only for lawful purposes. Prohibited behaviour includes, but is not limited to, breaching local or international laws, uploading defamatory or offensive material, attempting to gain unauthorised access to our servers or databases (including bypassing Cloudflare security layers), and sending unsolicited promotional material.</p>
            <p><strong>Intellectual Property:</strong> All content on our website, including text, graphics, logos, images, and software, is the property of NLI or its content suppliers and is protected by Irish and international copyright laws. You may not reproduce, distribute, or use any content for commercial purposes without our prior written consent.</p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">4. Events and Programs</h2>
            <p><strong>Registration and Communication:</strong> When registering for events, programmes, or other services, you agree to provide accurate and complete information. By signing up, your automated notifications and confirmation emails will be securely handled via our communications infrastructure (including Brevo).</p>
            <p><strong>Pricing & Conduct:</strong> All prices (where applicable) are quoted in Euro (EUR) and are inclusive of VAT. Many of our events and services are offered free of charge, in keeping with our mission. All participants are expected to behave respectfully. We reserve the right to remove any participant whose behaviour is disruptive or inconsistent with our core values, without refund.</p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">5. Branch Network</h2>
            <p>
                Individuals or groups interested in opening a branch of New Life Integration & Wellbeing Network must apply through our official process and agree to operate in accordance with our guidelines, values, and standards. Branch approval is at our sole discretion. NLI reserves the right to revoke branch status if these standards are not maintained.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">6. Grant and Consulting Services</h2>
            <p>
                NLI provides information, guidance, and support in applying for grants and funding opportunities. All grant-related guidance is provided for general informational purposes and does not constitute professional financial or legal advice. We do not guarantee the success of any grant application.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">7. Privacy and Data Protection</h2>
            <p>
                Your use of our website and services is also governed by our Privacy Policy, which explains how we collect, use, and protect your personal data via systems like Cloudflare, Brevo, and Google Tag Manager in accordance with the GDPR and Irish data protection law.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
            <p>
                To the fullest extent permitted by Irish law, our website and services are provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. NLI, along with our infrastructure partners (Cloudflare, Google), do not guarantee that the website will be completely uninterrupted, error-free, or free from external security vulnerabilities. Information provided through our services is for general informational purposes only and does not constitute professional advice.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">9. Photography and Recording</h2>
            <p>
                We may photograph or record our events and programmes for promotional, educational, or archival purposes. By attending our events, you consent to being photographed or recorded. If you do not wish to be included, please inform the event organiser. Images and recordings may be used on our website, social media, and marketing materials.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">10. Modifications to Terms</h2>
            <p>
                We reserve the right to update or modify these Terms and Conditions at any time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated "Last updated" date. Your continued use of our website and services after any changes constitutes your acceptance of the revised terms.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mt-4">11. Governing Law</h2>
            <p>
                These Terms and Conditions are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the Republic of Ireland. Any disputes arising out of or in connection with these terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of the Republic of Ireland.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

</Layout>